  = help: keep two values with `where`, or make one variable of two values from this one with `case`

error[Z0401]: `mcnemar_test` compares two variables of the same two values, but `b` has 3: x, y and z
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:67
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = ["x", "y", "z", "x"]).mcnemar_test(a, b)
  |                                                                   ^ more than two values
