error[Z0401]: frequency weights are whole numbers, but `w` has 1 fraction in row 1
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:91
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = [1, 0, 0, 1], w = [1.5, 1, 1, 1]).mcnemar_test(a, b, weights: w, weight_type: frequency)
  |                                                                                           ^ a frequency weight counts rows
  |
  = help: a weight with fractions is an analytic or a sampling weight: `weight_type: analytic`

error[Z0411]: `weights:` of `mcnemar_test` are sampling weights, which a test cannot use
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:89
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = [1, 0, 0, 1], w = [1, 1, 1, 1]).mcnemar_test(a, b, weights: w)
  |                                                                                         ^ sampling weights
  |
  = help: a regression with robust standard errors gives design-based inference, `reg(y ~ 1, weights: w, se: robust)`; frequency or analytic weights are taken with `weight_type: frequency` or `weight_type: analytic`

error[Z0401]: `mcnemar_test` counts pairs, so its weights are frequency weights, not analytic
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:105
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = [1, 0, 0, 1], w = [1, 1, 1, 1]).mcnemar_test(a, b, weights: w, weight_type: analytic)
  |                                                                                                         ^^^^^^^^ analytic weights on counts
  |
  = help: write `weight_type: frequency` for weights that say how many pairs each row stands for

error[Z0406]: `mcnemar_test` needs `b`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:43
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = [1, 0, 0, 1]).mcnemar_test(a)
  |                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^ `b` is missing
  |
  = help: usage: `data.mcnemar_test(a, b, correct: Bool = true, method: chi2 | exact = chi2, weights: Var, weight_type: frequency | analytic | sampling = sampling)`

error[Z0101]: no variable `c` in `the frame`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:59
  |
1 | frame(a = [1, 0, 1, 0], b = [1, 0, 0, 1]).mcnemar_test(a, c)
  |                                                           ^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: the variables of `the frame` are: a, b

